{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses and Aaron: This is the statute of the Passover</b> — This passage was spoken on the fourteenth of Nisan, in the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 12:43). And so indeed is the matter, for it is written at its end (Exodus 12:50), \"And all the children of Israel did as YHWH commanded,\" to teach about them that they and their servants were circumcised. And if so, it would have been fitting to place this passage before \"And it came to pass at midnight\" (Exodus 12:29). But the reason is that the passage \"This month shall be to you\" was spoken on the first of the month, and on that very day Moses immediately carried out his mission: \"And Moses called for all the elders of Israel and said to them\" (Exodus 12:21) — he commanded them in the statute of the Passover and promised them that they would be redeemed on the night of the fifteenth, and they believed: \"And the people bowed their heads and worshipped\" (Exodus 12:27). And Scripture placed next to this \"And it came to pass at midnight\" to say that He fulfilled His promise to them, and when this was completed, He returned to the earlier matter to complete the statute of the Passover.\n\nAnd this passage added many commandments: the prohibition of the stranger and the uncircumcised, and removal from the house, and breaking a bone, and the Passover of the convert — and they are commandments for immediate observance and for all generations. And He completed with it the statement that the children of Israel did all this and did as YHWH commanded. And He said here, \"all the children of Israel,\" to explain that there was not among them a single one who transgressed the word of YHWH in any of these matters and in all that He commanded in the laws of the Passover in all the mentioned passages.\n\nAnd Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 12:43) said that this passage concerning the Passover of generations was spoken after the Passover of Egypt, and he said, \"And the children of Israel did,\" refers to the wilderness Passover that they performed in the second year, and it was written here together with the commandment, in the manner of \"And Aaron placed it before the Testimony to be kept\" (Exodus 16:34). And this is a mistake, for they were not commanded in all these passages except concerning the Passover of Egypt and the Passovers of the Land, as is said above (Exodus 12:25), \"And it shall be when you come to the Land,\" etc. — but the wilderness Passover is a commandment that they were commanded in that chapter (of Numbers)." "<b>Every alien (בן נכר)</b> — whose deeds have become alienated from his Father in heaven; both a gentile and an Israelite are included in the meaning. Language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 12:43) from Mekhilta (here). And Scripture had no need except for an Israelite. And so Onkelos translated (Onkelos on Exodus 12:43) <b>כָּל בֶּן נֵכָר</b> — \"every son of Israel who apostatizes (דְּאִשְׁתַּמַּד)\": one who became alienated from his brother and from his Father in heaven through his evil deeds. And this is the apostate (משומד) that the Sages mentioned everywhere, and its meaning is \"made alien,\" and its Aramaic form is מְשֻׁמְדָּע, from the language of \"And Joseph made himself known (וְאִשְׁתְּמוֹדַע) to his brothers, but they did not make themselves known (אִשְׁתְּמוֹדְעוּהִי) to him\" (Genesis 42:8), and they dropped the ע — just as they elided it in many words, and they said מִדָּם in place of מִדָּעַם (see Arukh, entry מדעם): \"דּוֹר קְטִי\" (Ketuvot 10b) — meaning דּוֹר קְטִיעַ; \"בָּקִי\" — meaning בָּקִיעַ (Sanhedrin 5b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The final reference to Numbers is to the Passover observed in the second year in the wilderness, Numbers 9.", 1 "Ramban traces the Aramaic root of משומד (apostate) back to אשתמודע (to make oneself known/recognized), arguing the ע was elided, and supports this by citing parallel cases of consonant dropping in rabbinic literature."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:31.744913978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}